# ReceiptRadar - Project Overview

ReceiptRadar is a mobile application built with React Native (Expo + TypeScript) that allows users to:
- Upload shopping receipts via camera or gallery
- Store receipts in a personal receipt history
- Analyze spending patterns (monthly, per store)
- Contribute anonymized price data to a crowdsourced grocery price database
- Build shopping lists
- Find the cheapest store for their shopping list using price optimization

## Current Focus: Frontend Mobile App

**Important**: The current development phase focuses exclusively on the mobile app frontend. Backend API and database integration will be implemented later (likely .NET API + PostgreSQL).

## Core Architecture Principles

- **Frontend-First**: Build complete mobile app with local state management
- **Clean Architecture**: Separate concerns with clear service layers
- **Scalable Data Models**: Design for growth and future features
- **Modular Services**: Reusable, testable service components
- **Privacy First**: Anonymize price data contributions (when backend is integrated)
- **Type Safety**: Full TypeScript coverage

## Development Phases

### Phase 1 (Current - Frontend MVP)
- Mobile app UI/UX implementation
- Dummy login page (authentication deferred - no real auth yet)
- Receipt upload (camera/gallery) - local storage/mock
- OCR placeholder service (mock implementation)
- Receipt history and detail views (local state)
- Basic analytics dashboard (local data)
- Shopping list management (local state)
- Price optimization UI (mock data)

### Phase 2 (Future - Backend Integration)
- Backend API integration (likely .NET API)
- Database integration (PostgreSQL)
- Real authentication system (TBD - email, OAuth, etc.)
- Cloud storage for receipt images
- Real price observation creation
- Server-side price optimization

### Future Extensions
- Barcode scanning
- Automatic email receipt import
- Location-based pricing
- Improved AI receipt parsing
